  "question": {
    "text": "Electronic configuration of four elements $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{C}$ and D are given below :<br />(A) $1 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{p}^3$<br />(B) $1 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{p}^4$<br />(C) $1 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{p}^5$<br />(D) $1 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{p}^2$<br />Which of the following is the correct order of increasing electronegativity (Pauling's scale)?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "A &lt; D &lt; B &lt; C",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "A &lt; C &lt; B &lt; D",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "A &lt; B &lt; C &lt; D",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "D &lt; A &lt; B &lt; C",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{N}:-1 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{p}^3$ (Electronegativity $\\left.=3\\right)$<br />$\\mathrm{O}:-1 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{p}^4$ (Electronegativity $=3.5$)<br />$\\mathrm{F}:-1 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{p}^5$ (Electronegativity $=4$)<br />$\\mathrm{C}:-1 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{p}^2$ (Electronegativity $=2.55$)<br />Correct order $=\\mathrm{C} \\gt \\mathrm{B} \\gt \\mathrm{A} \\gt \\mathrm{D}$"
  }
